in this video i'm gonna explain the  warhammer titan which is the newest  titan shifter to be referenced  in the attack on titan anime it was  first mentioned during the second  episode of the final season  and is known to be possessed by a member  of the tiber family  since the great titan war over a hundred  years ago the warhammer  has never been used in battle and this  is partly the reason why the tiber  family is so respected worldwide  today we'll examine the warhammer  titan's strengths its weaknesses  and its various designs throughout  history big spoiler warning for those of  you who'd rather wait for the anime to  reveal this information  but for the rest of you let's get into  it and don't forget to sub for more  videos like this  okay so starting with the warhammer  titans strengths it's able to use a  special type of hardening that lets you  create a variety of weapons the weapons  it makes will usually manifest inside  its hands  as we saw in the trailer for season 4  how it conjured up a hammer  literally out of thin air this type of  hardening is special because  it actually has a degree of flexibility  as shown when it created a crossbow  which  of course requires an elastic string to  make it functional  normal titan hardening just does not  work that way so the warhammer has the  advantage  of being able to make flexible long  range weapons like whips or crossbows  this titan can also cause structures to  shoot out of the ground  such as this giant pillar that it made  or the spikes which look very similar to  stepping on a lego brick  in the entirety of the series so far as  of making this video the warhammer has  used its power to create a trident  a whip a crossbow a hammer a sword not  to mention conjuring spikes out of its  own body  out of the ground and obviously that  giant spiky pillow that i just mentioned  moving on to the warhammer's other  ability it's been long established that  the user of a titan shifter  can be found in the back of the titan's  neck but this is not always the case  when it comes to the warhammer  the user of this titan can choose to  encase themselves in a crystal  just like the one that annie is in and  then remotely control the warhammer  titan whilst inside it  there's a cable that connects the body  of the warhammer titan to the person in  the crystal  but the downside is that if this cable  is cut then the warhammer immediately  loses connection and becomes lifeless  the user can still make a new cable from  within the crystal and this will create  a new warhammer titan  however whilst the cable is vulnerable  the crystal itself is virtually  impossible to break into  which protects the user from something  like this happening to them  this titan's main weakness is that if it  creates too many structures in a short  space of time  then it will use up all its stamina and  be unable to make anything else  general mcgath outright said that the  power of the warhammer is quickly  exhausted  and we saw this play out during its  first appearance in the series  during its first fight the warhammer  made a ton of weapons  only for it to run out of energy after  about i'd probably say like 10 minutes  it's other weakness if you can call it  that is that its special hardening is  not indestructible  so it can be broken by other titan  shifters you know with repeated punches  or by biting with that said the  warhammer's design has several unique  features that separate it from other  titans  and thanks to some throwbacks in the  manga we've gotten glimpses of the  different warhammer titans throughout  history  one thing they all have in common is  that their flesh is covered in a thin  layer  of special hardening with enough space  for their eyes and mouth to be seen  the markings that we saw on the  warhammer titan's nape are reminiscent  of the markings that appear on the  on the user of a regular titan shifter  the user of the warhammer titan never  gets any markings on their actual face  because they're  obviously they're inside this crystal so  judging by the similarity of these two  lines  i'd imagine that it was just a visual  choice to put it on the titan itself  one of the former titans had these lines  on its face and another one had it along  its weird cape this warhammer  specifically had the freakiest design  but when you consider what i mentioned  earlier about how it has elastic  hardening that is flexible  you can understand why a titan like this  existed in the past  additionally another thing that makes  this titan stand out is the fact that  its body does not have to materialize  from the neck  like other titans do instead the  warhammer's body materializes from  whichever body part the cable is  connected to  in this clip we see how the warhammer is  taking shape from the bottom  upwards and that's because the cable was  attached to its foot in this moment  in a different situation the warhammer  can materialize from its head or any  other body part as long as that's where  the cable is attached  anyway guys that was the warhammer titan  explained and obviously if you've  watched this far i'm assuming you don't  care too much about spoilers  so if you want to know who has this  titan in the anime then it is the  sister of willie tiber so she was very  you know  when she first appeared in the anime she  was very much in the background she was  very easy to miss  i'm pretty sure she even had her eyes  closed um but yeah she was the person  who was selected  and when you think about it it makes  sense because willie tiber is meant to  be the head of the family right  and so if he has the warhammer then he's  gonna die within 13 years it's not great  so you'd rather have a head of the  family  that can stay in that position for a  really long time hence why it didn't  really make sense for him to have this  titan  be sure to drop a like if you like this  video and have a happy new year because  i will be posting this on the final day  of 2020 until 2021 peace out
 

